<p>Australia has granted humanitarian visas to five members of Iran’s national women’s soccer team after the players sought protection while in Australia for the Asian Cup, saying they feared for their safety if they returned to Iran. The situation escalated after Iranian state media criticized the athletes and branded them “traitors” for not singing the national anthem before a match in Australia. Australian officials said law enforcement and security agencies helped ensure the players’ safety and supported the process before the visa decision was finalized. President Donald Trump publicly urged Prime Minister Anthony Albanese to offer asylum and said he had spoken with Albanese about the situation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3ZkYXwt7G_XkITJL6ZsWCPhDkV_uGnKdbyTvNVvUxN9sYeCTFI8lz0sfzAmyExygqBERCgzjl2yR6R6EndYIlMvG-463Z04Pw8JG1BjefZMLx8CyEvfU_XR5iMdSIYupsc32wZtrIti3UnikDB1N394DnZzFVyvLksgS_8rsjCyWy1z65rk7KWc-nhUpPy_tCvjAB9TYYZl-l23LtQ309o72zbrTQXdUF_sK6usRwiLhLMMO5DUryEOhHeWx-21_YwjNncWQiocMU63ARQ' alt='Iranian players react from the bench during the women’s Asia Cup match on Australia’s Gold Coast.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Alarm signal: Advocates pointed to what looked like an “SOS” hand signal from players after their final Asian Cup match as a sign they needed protection.</li><li>Where the team was staying: Reports said the squad was staying at the Royal Pines resort on the Gold Coast and was due to leave Australia later in the week.</li><li>Hotel extraction details: Australia’s interior minister said police took five players from the team’s hotel before visas were granted, after consulting security agencies and amid reports that Iranian government minders were accompanying the squad.</li><li>Captain named: Reuters reporting cited by Al-Monitor said the five included team captain Zahra Ghanbari.</li><li>Pressure from groups: The Australian Iranian Council wrote to Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke urging protection for the players, while AUSIRAN called for private meetings with athletes away from “handlers” so they could safely express what they wanted.</li></ul><blockquote>I do know that the president called the prime minister and the views of the president put on this, I think, reflected what all good people have been thinking. - Tony Burke</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Australian government (Tony Burke): Burke said the women faced a difficult decision, and described “joy” and “relief” once visas were confirmed. He said the Australian Federal Police moved them to a safe location after consulting Australia’s security services. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/mar/10/iran-football-team-tony-burke-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-oil-price-inflation-federal-parliament-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump warned the players could be killed if they were forced back to Iran, urged Albanese to grant asylum, and later said five had been “taken care of,” while some might still return because of threats to family members. (<a href='https://time.com/7383247/trump-iran-womens-soccer-team-australia/'>Time</a>)</li><li>AUSIRAN (Rana Dadpour): Dadpour urged private meetings with players away from “handlers,” saying they needed support and could face execution if they returned to Iran. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-urges-australia-to-give-iran-womens-team-asylum/'>michaelwest.com.au</a>)</li><li>Amnesty International: Amnesty said some players faced “serious risks to their safety,” and urged Australia to protect them while they were in the country. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/mar/10/iran-football-team-tony-burke-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-oil-price-inflation-federal-parliament-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/trump-urges-australia-to-give-iran-womens-team-asylum/'>Trump urges Australia to give Iran women’s team asylum</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/world/australia/iran-soccer-womens-team-australia.html'>Australia Grants Humanitarian Visas to 5 Members of Iranian Women’s Soccer Team</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-war-womens-soccer-team-australia-dubbed-traitors-asian-cup-national-anthem/'>5 Iranian soccer players who sought asylum in Australia allowed to stay</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iranian-women-soccer-players-hotel-escape-aided-australian-police'>Iranian women soccer players&#x27; hotel escape aided by Australian police</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/watch-iran-womens-soccer-team-players-granted-visas-in-australia-amid-safety-fears/article70725337.ece'>Watch: Iran women’s soccer team players granted visas in Australia amid safety fears</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/mar/10/iran-football-team-tony-burke-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-oil-price-inflation-federal-parliament-ntwnfb'>Australia politics live: Iranian women’s football team arrive at Gold Coast airport as Amnesty says players face ‘serious risks to their safety’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/australia-5-iran-national-team-players-granted-asylum/a-76284734'>Australia: 5 Iran national team players granted asylum</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/03/09/trump-confirms-australia-will-grant-asylum-to-five-iranian-women-football-players'>Trump confirms Australia will grant asylum to five Iranian women football players</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-09-0700/donald-trump-trump-calls-australia-give-asylum-iranian-womens-soccer-players'>Trump calls on Australia to give asylum to Iranian women&#x27;s soccer players</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7383247/trump-iran-womens-soccer-team-australia/'>Trump Champions Protections for Iranian Women’s Soccer Team</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/10/g-s1-113146/australia-grants-asylum-to-5-members-of-the-iranian-womens-soccer-team'>Australia grants asylum to 5 members of the Iranian women&#x27;s soccer team</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iranian-womens-soccer-players-given-asylum-after-trump-speaks-with/'>Iranian women’s soccer players given asylum after Trump speaks with Australian PM</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/hes-on-it-trump-says-albanese-agrees-to-let-iranian-soccer-players-stay-in-australia-13987815.html'>‘He’s on it’: Trump says Albanese agrees to let Iranian soccer players stay in Australia</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy8e978xl8o'>Five Iranian footballers granted Australian visas after anthem protest</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>